### Plain Slate-Style Decoration Function

Source: https://github.com/udecode/plate/blob/main/docs/plans/2026-04-28-slate-v2-decoration-annotation-rewrite-review-plan.md

Defines a decoration function that finds search matches within text and returns them as decoration ranges. This is suitable for familiar, in-editor decoration needs.

```ts
const decorate = ({ entry, range, text }) => {
  return findSearchMatches(text, query).map((match) => ({
    anchor: { path: entry.path, offset: match.start },
    focus: { path: entry.path, offset: match.end },
    type: "search",
  }));
};
```

--------------------------------

### Create Decoration Source for High-Scale Decorations

Source: https://github.com/udecode/plate/blob/main/docs/plans/2026-04-28-slate-v2-decoration-annotation-rewrite-review-plan.md

Example of creating a decoration source for external or high-scale decoration needs. It requires an ID and a read function to fetch ranges, and an invalidates function to specify when decorations should be recomputed.

```ts
const searchDecorations = createDecorationSource(editor, {
  id: "search",
  read({ state, scope }) {
    return searchIndex.rangesFor(scope);
  },
  invalidates(change) {
    return change.textChanged || queryChanged;
  },
});
```

--------------------------------

### Refreshing external decoration source

Source: https://github.com/udecode/plate/blob/main/docs/plans/2026-05-18-slate-v2-external-decoration-sources-dx-ralplan.md

This code shows the process of mirroring state into `externalSnapshotRef`, writing React state separately, and then calling `externalSource.refresh()` to update decorations. This is used for manual invalidation.

```typescript
const externalSnapshotRef = useRef<SlateProjection[]>([]);
const [reactState, setReactState] = useState<string>('');

// ... update externalSnapshotRef and reactState ...

externalSource.refresh({
  reason: 'external',
  sourceId: 'external-diagnostics',
});

```

### Find

Source: https://github.com/udecode/plate/blob/main/content/docs/(plugins)/(functionality)/find-replace.mdx

The FindReplacePlugin is responsible for storing search options and registering a leaf node for highlighting. The decoration function, decorateFindReplace, finds matches within an element's text children and returns Slate ranges. The SearchHighlightLeaf, typically provided by the UI, renders these decorated ranges. The application code is responsible for updating the search query and performing any text replacement actions.

--------------------------------

### Fix Code Block Language Rehighlight > Notes

Source: https://github.com/udecode/plate/blob/main/docs/plans/2026-03-26-fix-codeblock-language-rehighlight.md

This fix is package-level only and does not include any registry UI changes. The `redecorate` functionality is now available on the base `SlateExtensionPlugin` API, allowing shared plugins to call `editor.api.redecorate()` without local casts.

